// examples/swarm/swarm.ent, a shoot-'em-up with foes and shots in their
// thousands, compiles, alone and for all the cores: the close foes are
// an archetype of their own (their tag is `apart`), every shot is held
// against every one of them in a `for` inside a `for`, and those run on all the cores.
// So does the `for` that steers every foe: its body calls out (a root,
// a sine), so it is worth sharing out from far fewer entities on than
// one that only computes. Running it needs a window.
// RUN: ent-translate --import-ent %S/../../examples/swarm/swarm.ent \
// RUN:     -I %S/../../devices -I %S/../../examples -o %t.mlir
// RUN: FileCheck %s --check-prefix=IR --input-file=%t.mlir
// RUN: ent-opt %t.mlir --ent-infer-archetypes | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=KINDS
// RUN: ent-opt %t.mlir --ent-lower-to-loops --cse --ent-lower-views \
// RUN:     --convert-scf-to-cf --convert-to-llvm --reconcile-unrealized-casts \
// RUN:     -o /dev/null
// RUN: ent-opt %t.mlir --ent-schedule \
// RUN:     --ent-lower-to-loops="fuse-systems=1 parallel-entities=1 parallel-stages=1" \
// RUN:     --symbol-dce --convert-scf-to-openmp --canonicalize --ent-omp-nowait \
// RUN:     -o %t.par.mlir
// RUN: FileCheck %s --check-prefix=PAR --input-file=%t.par.mlir
// (And on to LLVM: a body with a loop of its own is in no scope that
// would keep the loop from becoming blocks.)
// RUN: ent-opt %t.par.mlir --cse --ent-lower-views --convert-scf-to-cf \
// RUN:     --convert-to-llvm --reconcile-unrealized-casts -o /dev/null

// IR:     ent.component @Close () apart capacity 250000
// IR:     ent.system @strike()
// IR:       ent.query
// IR:         ent.each

// KINDS: ent.archetype @At_Foe_Health_Size (@At, @Foe, @Health, @Size) capacity 250000 inferred
// KINDS: ent.archetype @At_Foe_Health_Size_Close (@At, @Foe, @Health, @Size, @Close) capacity 250000 inferred

// PAR-LABEL: func.func private @steer(
// PAR:         omp.parallel
// PAR-LABEL: func.func private @gather(
// PAR-LABEL: func.func private @strike(
// PAR:         omp.parallel
// PAR:           omp.loop_nest
// PAR-NOT:         memref.alloca_scope
// PAR:             scf.for
// PAR-LABEL: func.func private @spend(
// PAR:         omp.parallel
